[0.000, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[2;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;205;146;2mUpdate Available\u001b[39m\u001b[22m                                                                                                                                                                 \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[3;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[38;2;158;158;158mNew version 1.3.0 is available. Run \u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;189;127;231mpi update\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b"]
[0.000, "o", "[4;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[38;2;158;158;158mChangelog: \u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;189;127;231mhttps://pi.dev/changelog\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                              \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[6;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[7;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[8;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m \u001b[39mwhere are you running?                                                                                                                                                           \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[9;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[11;1H\u001b[2K I’m running in \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m/workspace\u001b[39m, inside the pi coding-agent environm"]
[0.000, "o", "ent.                                                                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[12;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mWe need answer where running. Need maybe inspect cwd? We know cwd /workspace from system. User asks where are you running? Could answer in /workspace. Maybe mention pi coding   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[13;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;151;151;151magent harness. Need concise. We can say I'm running in the current working directory \u001b[39m\u001b[23m\u001b[38;2;189;127;231m/workspace\u001b[39m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151m, inside the pi coding-agent environment. No need tools. Final only.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m              \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[15;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[16;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m \u001b[39mI'm running in a sandbox and my user can close their computer and this will keep running                            "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                             \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[17;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[19;1H\u001b[2K Got it — so the sandbox keeps running independently of the local machine. That means:                                                                                            \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[20;1H\u001b[2K                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[21;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m- \u001b[39mLong-running commands or builds won't die if the laptop closes.                                                                                                                \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[22;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m- \u001b[39mAnything I write to the filesystem (e.g., under \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m/"]
[0.001, "o", "workspace\u001b[39m) persists between interactions.                                                                                     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[23;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m- \u001b[39mI don't have memory across sessions beyond what's in files, so if you want something remembered, I should write it down.                                                       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[25;1H\u001b[2K Want me to do anything with that in mind — like kick off a long task, or set up notes/state files for continuity?                                                                \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[26;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mThe user is telling me they're running in a sandbox, and their user can close their computer and this (the sandbox/agent) will keep running. They seem to be making a statement, \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[27;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;151;151;151mperhaps wanting confirmation or discussion about what that means. There's no explicit question. I should respond concisely, acknowledging the setup: the sandbox persists        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[28;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[3;3"]
[0.000, "o", "8;2;151;151;151mindependently of the local machine, so long-running tasks can continue, sessions can be resumed, etc. Maybe note implications: I can run long commands, but I don't have         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[29;1H\u001b[2K \u001b[3;38;2;151;151;151mpersistent memory between sessions unless files are written; state persists in the filesystem of the sandbox. Keep it brief and conversational.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[30;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[31;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[32;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m \u001b[39mcreate a file called stream.txt and wrie to it \"hello world \" + timestamp every 3 seconds. run the writes to this file as a background job                                       \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\u001b[33;1H\u001b[2K\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                     "]
