[0.000, "o", "                              \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;205;146;2m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;A\u0007\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m \u001b[39mwhere are you running?                                                                                                                                         "]
[0.000, "o", "                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;B\u0007\u001b]133;C\u0007\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;A\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n I’m running in \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m/workspace\u001b[39m, inside the pi coding-agent environment.                                                                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mWe need answer where running. Need maybe inspect cwd? We know cwd /workspace from system. User asks where are you running? Could answer in /workspace. Maybe mention pi coding   \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;B\u0007\u001b]133;C\u0007 \u001b[3;38;2;151;151;151magent harness. Need concise. We can say I'm running in the current working directory \u001b[39m\u001b[23m\u001b[38;2;189;127;231m/workspace\u001b[39m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151m, inside the pi coding-agent environment. No need tools. Final only.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m              \u001b[0m"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;A\u0007\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m \u001b[39mI'm running in a sandbox and my user can close their computer and this will keep running                                                                                         \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;B\u0007\u001b]133;C\u0007\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;A\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n Got it — so the sandbox keeps running independently of the local machine. That means:                                                                                            \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                              "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m- \u001b[39mLong-running commands or builds won't die if the laptop closes.                                                                                                                \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m- \u001b[39mAnything I write to the filesystem (e.g., under \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m/workspace\u001b[39m) persists between interactions.                                                                                     \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m- \u001b[39mI don't have memory across sessions beyond what's in files, so if you want something remembered, I should write it down.                                                       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n Want me to do anything with that in mind — like kick off a long task, or set up notes/state file"]
[0.000, "o", "s for continuity?                                                                \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mThe user is telling me they're running in a sandbox, and their user can close their computer and this (the sandbox/agent) will keep running. They seem to be making a statement, \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3;38;2;151;151;151mperhaps wanting confirmation or discussion about what that means. There's no explicit question. I should respond concisely, acknowledging the setup: the sandbox persists        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3;38;2;151;151;151mindependently of the local machine, so long-running tasks can continue, sessions can be resumed, etc. Maybe note implications: I can run long commands, but I don't have         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;B\u0007\u001b]133;C\u0007 \u001b[3;38;2;151;151;151mpersistent memory between sessions unless files are written; state persists in the filesystem of the sandbox. Keep it brief and conversational.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;A\u0007\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                  "]
[0.001, "o", "                                                                                                                                                                \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m \u001b[39mcreate a file called stream.txt and wrie to it \"hello world \" + timestamp every 3 seconds. run the writes to this file as a background job                                       \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;B\u0007\u001b]133;C\u0007\u001b[48;2;0;51;70m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mThe user wants a background job that appends \"hello world \" + timestamp to stream.txt every 3 seconds. I should create the file and start a background loop with nohup or        \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3;38;2;151;151;151msimilar so it keeps running after the bash tool call returns.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                                                   "]
[0.000, "o", "                                 \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mI'll use a bash command with nohup and & to detach it. Something like:\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                                                                           \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mnohup bash -c 'while true; do echo \"hello world \u001b[39m\u001b[23m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151m$(date)\" >> /workspace/stream.txt; sleep 3; done' > /dev/null 2>&1 &\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                   "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                               \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mThen verify it's running and the file is being written. Let me do it in steps: start the job, then check after a few seconds.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                    \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[39m\u001b[1m$ touch /workspace/stream.txt && nohup bash -c 'while true; do echo \"hello world $(date +\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\")\" >> /workspace/stream.txt; sleep 3; done' > /dev/null 2>&1 & echo  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[1m\"started PID $!\"\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                 \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m                                    "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                                                                                              \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[38;2;158;158;158mstarted PID 799\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[38;2;158;158;158mTook 0.1s\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                        \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m                                                                                                                                                                    "]
[0.000, "o", "              \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mStarted. Now verify it's writing — wait a few seconds and read the file.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                                                                         \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[39m\u001b[1m$ sleep 8 && cat /workspace/stream.txt && ps aux | grep -v grep | grep \"stream.txt\" | head -2\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                                    \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[38;2;158;158;158m... (3 earlier lines,\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;129;129;129mctr"]
[0.000, "o", "l+o\u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;158;158;158m to expand\u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;158;158;158m)\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                          \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[38;2;158;158;158mhello world 2026-10-19 05:58:22\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[38;2;158;158;158mhello world 2026-10-19 05:58:25\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[38;2;158;158;158m  799 sandbox   0:00 /bin/bash -c touch /workspace/stream.txt && nohup bash -c 'while true; do echo \"hello world $(date +\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\")\" >> /workspace/stream.txt; sleep   \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[38;2;158;158;158m3; done' > /dev/null 2>&1 & echo \"started PID $!\"\u001b[39m        "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                                                                        \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[38;2;158;158;158m  801 sandbox   0:00 bash -c while true; do echo \"hello world $(date +\"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S\")\" >> /workspace/stream.txt; sleep 3; done\u001b[39m                                              \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m \u001b[38;2;158;158;158mTook 8.0s\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                        \u001b[49m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;37;52;14m                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\u001b[0"]
[0.000, "o", "m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;A\u0007\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n Done. The background job is running and appending to \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m/workspace/stream.txt\u001b[39m every 3 seconds:                                                                                      \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mLoop PID:\u001b[22m 801 (detached via \u001b[38;2;189;127;231mnohup\u001b[39m, so it survives this session)                                                                                                                \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[38;2;189;127;231m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mOutput so far:\u001b[22m 5 lines and growing, e.g. \u001b[38;2;189;127;231mhello world 2026-10-19 05:58:25\u001b[39m                                                                                                       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                           "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                                       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n To stop it later: \u001b[38;2;189;127;231mkill 801\u001b[39m (or \u001b[38;2;189;127;231mpkill -f stream.txt\u001b[39m).                                                                                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b]133;B\u0007\u001b]133;C\u0007 \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;151;151;151mIt's working. The background loop (PID 801) is appending every 3 seconds. Report concisely, including how to stop it.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                            \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;126;167;66m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[38;2;126;167;66m\u001b[1m$ ls\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                             \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n                                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[38;2;158;158;158mstream.txt\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                       \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n \u001b[38;2;158;158;158m\u001b[39m                                                                                                                                                                                 \u001b[0m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[38;2;126;167;66m────────"]
